@@ -0,0 +1,232 @@
+FOMOD SOURCE AND PACKAGING NOTES
+================================
+
+These technical notes and SOURCE_MANIFEST.json remain in the repository
+and build output. The user ZIP contains installation instructions and credits.
+
+LAYOUT
+------
+The canonical source for shared helpers, UI and existing RC7/WearableDevices
+overrides remains extras/dlss_gamma/gamedata. The FOMOD builder routes those
+files into separate components instead of installing them all unconditionally.
+
+Since 0.63 the patch replaces no ssfx_* shader (AO, IL, SSR, SSS, SSS-ext,
+water SSR). Earlier versions added an upscaler jitter offset to their history
+lookups, plus a per-tile noise offset in Atmospherics GTAO. A side-by-side
+test showed no visible difference, and the overrides had to track every SSS /
+Atmospherics release (RC7.7 reworked these shaders and broke the RC7.x set).
+SSS and Atmospherics now always use their own. The removed overrides remain
+in git history if the GTAO noise offset is ever needed again.
+
+extras/dlss_fomod/sss235 contains SSS 23.5's deffer_impl_flat.ps with motion
+vectors, installed by the mandatory base component. The RC7.x choice replaces
+it with Atmospherics' version at priority 100. WearableDevices is installed
+only when selected, with priority 200.
+
+The Better Beef's checkbox installs its three shader overrides at priority
+200. When combined with RC7.x, a conditional priority-300 merge replaces only
+combine_2_naa.ps. With the checkbox off, none of these overrides is installed.
+
+The original flat extras/dlss_gamma payload is retained for existing release
+workflows. It is still the RC7-oriented patch; it is not the SSS-only variant.
+Use tools/dlss/package_compatibility.py to build the new multi-variant FOMOD.
+
+BASE SOURCES
+------------
+Source archive: ScreenSpaceShaders_Update23_5.zip
+SHA256: f442e925248620451b525ac037b0a58b9bd97303abcecc695d600b71884025b4
+
+SSS archive members and the corresponding installed GAMMA files matched
+when preparing this package. Individual input and output hashes are recorded
+in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json.
+
+deffer_impl_flat.ps:
+  Source: 05 - Rain - Puddles/gamedata/shaders/r3/deffer_impl_flat.ps
+  Add the motion-vector header and assign O.velocity before returning.
+  Keep SSS's 0.95 terrain material and 0.6 normal-strength values; do not copy
+  Atmospherics' material sentinel or normal-strength changes into this file.
+  SSS's Puddles module replaces the MV main file's version and drops the
+  velocity output; without it flat ground has no motion vectors.
+
+ATMOSPHERICS
+------------
+The installed stock GAMMA Atmospherics package identifies its source as
+Atmospherics_GAMMA_2.68.93_hotfix3.7z. It does not supply deffer_impl_flat.ps,
+so its choice retains the SSS base. Its separate sky shader includes
+night_vision.h, which is why the existing header remains in the shared base.
+
+Atmospherics 2.69 RC7.5, RC7.6, RC7.7 and RC7.71 share one choice. Their
+deffer_impl_flat.ps ("In common" in the RC7.7 / RC7.71 FOMODs) match after
+newline normalization, and the RC7.x component reuses the existing
+extras/dlss_gamma override (Atmospherics' file with motion vectors)
+byte-for-byte. It works with every AO / IL / SSR option in RC7.7 / RC7.71's
+installer, since none of them is touched. RC7.7 / RC7.71's combine_2_naa.ps
+differs from RC7.6 only in comments, so Better Beef's + RC7.x reuses
+better_beefs_atmos_rc7. RC7.71 shaders read the engine's ssfx_timedelta
+(frame time, frame number in .y), which these binaries bind.
+
+Atmospherics 2.69 RC8 has its own choice. Its deffer_impl_flat.ps ("In
+common") is byte-identical to RC7.71's, so the choice installs the same
+atmos_rc7 component. Its combine_2_naa.ps changed (sky-only debanding and a
+triangular dither from the new atmos_dither.h, which RC7.x lacks), so
+Better Beef's + RC8 installs better_beefs_atmos_rc8. RC8 replaces none of the
+base component's files. Its volumetric sun reads volume_range (set by the
+stock engine per sun cascade) and skips the near cascade; rain_apply_gloss.ps
+reads s_patched_normal, which the stock rain blender binds.
+
+RC8 hotfix 4 keeps the same deffer_impl_flat.ps (byte-identical) and adds no
+shader resources or constants. Its combine_2_naa.ps blends bloom with the new
+tonemap_add_sRGB (tonemap_sRGB.h, which also defines PBRN_WHITE) instead of
+blend_soft. better_beefs_atmos_rc8 now starts from hotfix 4's file and keeps
+blend_soft behind #ifndef PBRN_WHITE, so the one file serves RC8 before and
+after hotfix 4.
+
+GLOSSY PUDDLES OVERHAUL V2.5
+----------------------------
+Source: Glossy Puddles Overhaul v2.5 - Erandis (local FOMOD). Glossy Puddles
+replaces deffer_impl_flat.ps without the motion-vector output, so flat ground
+loses temporal motion under DLSS / FSR. Its FOMOD ships two distinct versions
+of that file: "PBR Puddles" (PBR Shader Based Weathers, both the SSS 23.5 and
+SSS 24 / RC3 folders are identical) and "SSS Puddles" (SSS Based Weathers,
+likewise identical across SSS versions).
+
+v2.4's two deffer_impl_flat.ps files match v2.3's after newline
+normalization, so the patched files are unchanged. v2.4 fixes Atmospherics
+RC8: v2.3's pbr_brdf_terrain.h lacks g_terrain_nv, which RC8's lmodel.h
+writes, so v2.3 above RC8 fails to compile most RC8 lighting shaders with or
+without this patch. v2.4 declares it.
+
+v2.5 adds footstep ripples: erandis_puddle_ripples.script feeds eight shader
+bus lanes (bus_erandis_ring0-7) and both deffer_impl_flat.ps files include the
+new erandis_puddle_ripples.h and add three lines for them. The patched files
+now start from v2.5, so they need v2.5 installed (the header is v2.5's) and no
+longer drop the ripples on flat ground. v2.5's terrain shader keeps its
+motion vectors; its SSR change guards its own SKY_TINT_GAIN.
+
+glossy_puddles_pbr / glossy_puddles_sss deffer_impl_flat.ps:
+  Add #include "screenspace_mvectors.h" and assign O.velocity before
+  returning, exactly as in the other deffer_impl_flat.ps variants. Nothing
+  else edited. A user-reported fix for the PBR version made the same change.
+  v2.3 changed only the PBR file: bus_erandis is now declared behind
+  GP_BUS_ERANDIS_DECLARED, because its settings_screenspace_PUDDLES.h also
+  declares it. Without that guard the PBR file fails to compile against
+  v2.3 and later. The SSS file is unchanged from v2.2.
+
+Every Atmospherics choice sets dlss_weather_family: pbr for RC7.x and RC8, sss
+otherwise. With the checkbox on, a conditional install at priority 250 picks
+the matching file. Its other files (scripts, terrain shader, SSR header) keep
+motion vectors or touch nothing this patch overrides and are not included.
+The shader_bus Lua API it uses is in these binaries (upstream 2026-10-11).
+
+WEARABLEDEVICES
+---------------
+The third page installs the existing wd_body.vs byte-for-byte when selected.
+No glow/bloom workaround, device draw-order change or engine rollback is
+included. The original mod itself is not bundled.
+
+BETTER BEEF'S NVGS
+------------------
+Source: BetterBeefsNVGs_indiesunpraiser.19 supplied for this integration.
+The linked ModDB page currently identifies its download as .18; the local
+supplied .19 files are the source of this patch, not an assumed web revision.
+Source members and byte hashes are recorded under better_beefs in the manifest.
+
+The previous compatibility header derives from stock Beef's NVG. Better
+Beef's generation shaders instead construct NVGParams and call nvg_process;
+the stock header does not supply that interface. Its .19 Lua scripts also
+pack extra per-generation settings that the stock header does not implement.
+
+better_beefs/night_vision.h:
+  Copy the full supplied 00 - Main header, retaining its controls/functions.
+  Add a depth GetDimensions query in blurred_depth and use the depth resource
+  dimensions for its two integer Load coordinates. Keep screen_res for colour,
+  noise, blur radius and display effects. This matches the existing stock NVG
+  correction: the engine runs phase_nightvision after reconstruction while
+  s_position remains at scene resolution. NVG processing stays native-sized.
+
+better_beefs/pp_blur.ps:
+  Start from 02 - PATCH - [ SSS ]. Keep its NVG half/quarter/eighth-res pipeline
+  and SSFX_Blur fallback. Use s_position.GetDimensions for the first half-res
+  pass's two depth loads. The current engine runs phase_blur before temporal
+  reconstruction, so this preserves the existing mapping there and avoids
+  assuming a colour-pass size for depth lookups. Blur pass selection/radii
+  retain screen_res, matching phase_blur's RenderScreenWidth/Height constants.
+
+better_beefs/combine_2_naa.ps:
+  Preserve the original 02 - PATCH - [ SSS ] file, including the condition
+  that excludes an active NVG lens from SSS LUT grading. Used with SSS-only
+  and stock Atmospherics, which does not supply this combine shader.
+
+better_beefs_atmos_rc7/combine_2_naa.ps:
+  Start with the installed Atmospherics RC7.6 file; the RC7.5 source is
+  identical after newline normalization. Add Better Beef's LUT-mask condition
+  around ssfx_lut_pp without removing Atmospherics clarity or final dithering.
+  Only installed when BOTH RC7.x and Better Beef's are selected.
+
+better_beefs_atmos_rc8/combine_2_naa.ps:
+  Start with Atmospherics RC8 hotfix 4's "In common" file, newlines
+  normalized. Add the same Better Beef's LUT-mask condition around
+  ssfx_lut_pp, keeping RC8's debanding and dither. Its two tonemap_add_sRGB
+  bloom lines fall back to RC8's blend_soft when PBRN_WHITE is not defined
+  (RC8 before hotfix 4). Only installed when BOTH RC8 and Better Beef's are
+  selected.
+
+The original mod remains responsible for its generation shaders, settings
+and Lua scripts, including its FDDA Redone patch where applicable. Its
+03 - PATCH - [ SSS Weapons DOF ] must remain installed when that SSS module
+is used; it preserves the mod's encoded-blur handling. That shader reads
+depth via SSFX_get_position and runs before reconstruction in this engine,
+so it is not overridden by this compatibility package.
+
+All four compatibility shaders retain original author comments/credits.
+No C++ changes, new runtime constants or extra rendering passes are added.
+This optional integration has not been shader-compiled or tried in-game.
+
+BUILD
+-----
+From the repository root with Python 3.10 or later:
+  python tools/dlss/package_compatibility.py
+
+Default output:
+  _build/releases/<VERSION>/
+
+Use --output with a new directory for another build. The builder refuses to
+overwrite an existing output directory. It packages only explicit shader/UI
+sources, instructions, selection records and the FOMOD XML. It does not read
+the user's current mod installation, compile shaders, run tests, launch MO2,
+change profiles or install binaries. Source archives are not needed to rebuild.
+
+The separate build MANIFEST.json lists archive member sizes and hashes.
+SOURCE_MANIFEST.json records provenance of the SSS, Atmospherics, Better
+Beef's and Glossy Puddles source files. Updating shader sources requires
+updating this provenance and the stated compatibility versions deliberately.
+
+STATUS
+------
+0.721: compatibility patch only, for the same 0.72 binaries. Glossy Puddles
+moves to v2.5 and Better Beef's + RC8 to RC8 hotfix 4 (with an RC8 fallback).
+Checked with fxc: the patch's own shaders compile and break none of the mods'
+shaders on RC8 hotfix 4 (both feature sets), hotfix 4 and original RC8 with
+Better Beef's, and Glossy Puddles v2.5 on hotfix 4 (PBR with both SSR choices),
+RC7.71, stock Atmospherics and SSS only. Not installed through MO2 or played.
+
+0.72: lmape.vs, dlss_volumetric_history.ps and the frame generation laser fill
+shaders join the base component, and Atmospherics RC8 gets its own choice. The
+patch's own shaders compile on SSS 23.5, stock Atmospherics, RC7.71 and RC8
+(with either feature set, or with Better Beef's), and break none of RC8's
+shaders. Glossy Puddles v2.4 compiles on all of these stacks (PBR with both
+SSR choices, SSS) and the patch breaks none of their shaders on top of it.
+This exact package was not installed through MO2.
+
+0.71: vert.vs joins the base component. The patch's own shaders compile on SSS 23.5,
+stock Atmospherics and RC7.71. This exact package was not installed through MO2,
+and the other installer choices were not exercised.
+
+0.7: the patch's own shaders compile on SSS 23.5, stock Atmospherics and RC7.71.
+The test build of this patch was installed through MO2 with the RC7.x choice and
+played; the other installer choices were not exercised.
+
+0.63: the three-page installer was installed through MO2 and the game loaded
+with it; not every option combination was exercised. SSS, stock Atmospherics
+and RC7.71 shaders compile on top of this patch, and the Glossy Puddles
